# Environment variables PyReverseETL actually reads. Source and destination
# credentials (Postgres/MySQL/S3/webhook/CRM) are NOT read from environment
# variables anywhere in this codebase - they're passed as JSON via
# `--source-config`/`--dest-config` on the CLI or the `source_config`/
# `destination_config` arguments to `pyreverseetl.run_sync()`. See the
# README "Quick start" section for real examples.
#
# The variables below are the only ones any code path in this repo reads
# (grep for `std::env::var` in core/src if you want to verify this yourself).

# --- StatGuardian quality-gate integration ---
# core/src/governance/credentials.rs: GovernanceCredentials::from_env()
# reads one of these. NOTE: per README.md ("Known gaps"), the StatGuardian
# quality-gate module is present in the codebase but is NOT wired into the
# real `execute_sync` sync path - setting these has no effect on `pyreverseetl
# execute` today.
STATGUARDIAN_TOKEN=
STATGUARDIAN_API_KEY=

# --- Test-only, used exclusively by the ignored Docker-backed integration
# tests (`cargo test -- --ignored`, see README "Development" section).
# Never read by the real sync path.
PYREVERSEETL_TEST_PG_PORT=5439
PYREVERSEETL_TEST_MYSQL_PORT=3307
PYREVERSEETL_TEST_MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
